OCCT V8_0_1, PLib.cxx: polynomial evaluation (PLib::EvalPolynomial, NoDerivativeEvalPolynomial) has a
fixed-size path per dimension up to THE_MAX_OPT_DIM and a slow runtime loop above it. B-spline evaluation
reaches dimensions above 15 (juno's build: 72.9 M of 230.5 M evaluations, mostly dimension 28);
48 keeps it on the fixed-size path, with results bit-identical. ocp.sh applies it to a copy of this one file
(`--plib-stock` leaves it out); every other OCCT file is compiled as released.

--- a/src/FoundationClasses/TKMath/PLib/PLib.cxx
+++ b/src/FoundationClasses/TKMath/PLib/PLib.cxx
@@ -711,7 +711,7 @@
 namespace
 {
 // Maximum dimension for optimized template dispatch
-constexpr int THE_MAX_OPT_DIM = 15;
+constexpr int THE_MAX_OPT_DIM = 48;

 // Evaluation of only value using local array (register-friendly).
 // Writes to output only at the end.
